<article class="env-lemma" id="08FE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08FE">Lemma <span data-tag="08FE">20.32.4</span>.</a> Let $f : (X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y)$ be a morphism of ringed spaces. Given an open subspace $V \subset Y$, set $U = f^{-1}(V)$ and denote $g : U \to V$ the induced morphism. Then $(Rf_*E)|_ V = Rg_*(E|_ U)$ for $E$ in $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Represent $E$ by a K-injective complex $\mathcal{I}^\bullet $ of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. Then $Rf_*(E) = f_*\mathcal{I}^\bullet $ and $Rg_*(E|_ U) = g_*(\mathcal{I}^\bullet |_ U)$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/08BS" data-tag="08BS">20.32.1</a>. Since it is clear that $(f_*\mathcal{F})|_ V = g_*(\mathcal{F}|_ U)$ for any sheaf $\mathcal{F}$ on $X$ the result follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>